# main + production

When you push shippable work to **`main`** in this repo (docs, integrations, SDK source that docs/Railway should show), **also update `production` in the same session** unless the user explicitly says main-only.

## Promote

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout production
git merge origin/main -m "Merge main: <short why>."
git push origin production
git checkout main
```

Prefer a merge commit when fast-forward is not possible (this repo’s history uses `Merge main: …`).

## Rules

- Railway docs / example-store / status deploy from **`production` only** — never point them at `main` (see `DEPLOY.md`).
- Package publishes and version tags still come from **`main`**.
- Do not leave docs or public integration changes on `main` without promoting `production` when the user expects the live site updated.
- Confirm both remotes after promote: `origin/main` is an ancestor of `origin/production` (or production tip contains the main tip).
